# /handoff

Write now — end of this stage, not task start. Keep routing recommendations and their brief reason only in the short unfenced header above `PROMPT:`. Write each field as its own paragraph with exactly one blank line between fields. Keep labels plain; bold the next stage and each model and effort value. The fenced prompt contains only what the receiving model needs to continue: task state, constraints, exposure/shape, checks, advisor accounting, and relevant delegation state. Do not duplicate header-only fields inside it.

## Active workflow contract

A user `/handoff` request or a received handoff activates the workflow through the stage chain. Skill loads do not carry between stages. Every receiving stage must freshly load `routing` before any action, must load `consult` before any advisor call, and must load this `handoff` skill only at END before writing the next handoff. Every handoff must carry the mandatory loads in its `PROMPT:` exactly as the skeleton shows.

For a legacy handoff containing only `RISK:`, classify the next concrete action into `EXPOSURE:` and `SHAPE:` at stage start. Do not inherit or translate the old workflow-wide maximum mechanically.

## Infer STAGE

| State | STAGE |
|---|---|
| no plan | Plan |
| unverified plan | Verify Plan |
| ready plan | Implement |
| implemented | Verify Implementation |

Without `/handoff`, work directly. Micro normally skips Plan and Verify Plan; Bounded may use an inline plan and skips separate verification unless a material decision remains. Skip a stage: same skeleton, add `SKIP TO: <stage>`, justify the skip.

## Skeleton

The header before `PROMPT:` is unfenced. Write each field as its own paragraph with exactly one blank line between fields—never combine fields on one line or in one paragraph. Keep field labels plain (e.g. write `NEXT:`, not `**NEXT:**`). Bold only the `NEXT` value and each model and effort value exactly as shown below (`**<model>**, **<effort>**`; keep `none` plain). Enclose only the content under `PROMPT:` in a ```md code fence.

REPO: <short label>

NEXT: **<next stage>**

PREFERRED: **<model>**, **<effort>**

SECONDARY: **<{{if .Both}}other-provider {{end}}model>**, **<effort>**

TERTIARY: **<model>**, **<effort>**

WHY: <brief routing reason>

ADVISORS: <none | N call(s), complete | N call(s): <nonzero buckets only, e.g. 1 complete, 1 failed (usage limit)> | unverified (<reason>); see CONSULT HISTORY>

STATE: <changed/committed/applied or blocked; one short line>

PROMPT:
```md
HANDOFF WORKFLOW: active
MANDATORY SKILLS:
- Load `routing` before any stage action; do not rely on a prior stage's load or summary.
- Load `consult` before any advisor call; loading it never requires a call.
- Load `handoff` only at END, immediately before writing the required next handoff.
REPO: <short label>
CURRENT STAGE: <stage>
EXPOSURE: <Local|Shared|Consequential; concrete next action and boundary>
SHAPE: <Micro|Bounded|Standard|Deep; basis>
TASK GOAL: <one sentence>
PLAN FILE: <repo-relative path or "not needed">
SPEC FILES: <repo-relative paths or "none known">
CONSULT BUDGET ID: <stable user-approved scope-envelope identifier>
CONSULT LIMIT: <completed batches cap>; <attempts cap>
CONSULT GRANTS: <each exact additional batch/attempt pair, user authorization and route/fallback restrictions, or none>
CONSULT LEDGER: <durable owner ledger path>
CONSULT STATE: <consistent|conflicted; evidence and frozen allowance if conflicted>
CONSULT USED: <completed_batches>/<cap> batches; <attempts_started>/<cap> attempts; preserve unknown/conflicting values explicitly>
