## Field semantics

| Field | Fill |
|---|---|
| REPO | label, not a path; or `none`. Repo-relative paths go inside the prompt |
| NEXT / CURRENT STAGE | receiving stage from Infer STAGE; NEXT is the short summary (bolded in header: `NEXT: **<stage>**`) |
| ADVISORS | human quick status; full accounting lives in CONSULT USED / CONSULT HISTORY. Calls = `attempts_started`. Write exactly one form: `none` (0 calls); `N call(s), complete` (all complete); `N call(s): ` + only non-zero buckets in order complete, partial, failed, each partial/failed with a short parenthesized reason; `unverified (<reason>); see CONSULT HISTORY` when history is missing or conflicting. Never write zero buckets or a trailing `none` (not `0 calls: 0 complete, 0 partial, 0 failed; none`) |
| STATE | one-line working/commit/deployment/blocker summary |
| EXPOSURE | exposure of the next concrete action: Local, Shared or Consequential; name the actual boundary, not a sensitive topic |
| SHAPE | task shape: Micro, Bounded, Standard or Deep; state the evidence that makes the low route checkable or requires more capability |
| PLAN FILE | repo-relative, or `not needed: simple task` |
| SPEC FILES | spec/design/requirements in-repo or from the user prompt; `none known` if absent — never omit the field |
| PREFERRED | one model + effort. Header format: `PREFERRED: **<model>**, **<effort>**`. One route, no competing plans. No clear best → stop and ask |
{{if .Both}}| SECONDARY | matched-capability other-provider model + effort. Match task capability, not effort names: Sol medium pairs with Opus low, Sol xhigh with Opus medium. Header format: `SECONDARY: **<{{if .Both}}other-provider {{end}}model>**, **<effort>**`. Impossible → say why in WHY |{{else}}| SECONDARY | a second suitable {{.OnlyProvider}} model or effort that matches the task's capability, or `none`. Header format: `SECONDARY: **<model>**, **<effort>**`. Only one provider is selected, so no other-provider route exists |{{end}}
| TERTIARY | third distinct suitable model, or `none`. Header format: `TERTIARY: **<model>**, **<effort>**` or `none`. {{if .Both}}The three together span at least two providers and never repeat a model.{{else}}The three never repeat a model and effort pair.{{end}} Do not add an expensive route merely to fill the field |
| CONSULT BUDGET ID | stable across the user-approved scope envelope, plan versions, stages, handoffs, Fix loops, owner changes, compaction, and elapsed time; only materially new user-approved scope creates a new ID |
| CONSULT LIMIT | resident cap: all scopes `1; 2`; Consequential scopes `2; 3`; plus exact user-authorized additions. Capacity is not a target |
| CONSULT USED | monotonic ledger counters: every issued launch request spends an attempt; substantive advice spends one batch, including partial advice. Neither agreement nor exit 0 controls charging. Conflicts freeze original remaining allowance until evidence resolves them; never choose whichever row permits a call |
| CONSULT GRANTS | retain each exact user-authorized batch/attempt addition, authorization, route/fallback restrictions, and any model-specific approval{{if .Codex}} such as an Astra grant{{end}}; no counter resets. A pending request is nonblocking for safe work, and a later grant is portable across stages in the same scope but never retroactive.{{if .Codex}} No Astra reply means not granted, not a general advisor block{{end}} |
| CONSULT LEDGER | durable owner-maintained path outside disposable worktrees; embed all accounting state here even if path is inaccessible to next owner |
| CONSULT STATE | consistent or conflicted; preserve original conflicting records, uncertainty and frozen allowance separately from explicit additional grants |
| CONSULT TRIGGER | exact resident-core trigger that fired, or `none`; allowance state and fallback are never triggers |
| CONSULT BATCH ID | stable across the initial attempt and its one permitted fallback; a fallback never creates a new batch |
| CONSULT SCOPE | decision checkpoint plus every then-known eligible boundary/question bundled into the batch |
| CONSULT STATUS | `not triggered` unless an exact resident-core trigger fired; exposure/shape/stage/unused capacity never trigger. Use `required`, `partial`, `covered`, or `exhausted` only with evidence; a charged batch need not cover all questions |
| ADVISOR ALLOWANCE HISTORY | newest-first selection evidence for every batch: batch ID, time, the declared plan behind the route order, and any usage-limit or unavailable-model messages observed; unobserved allowance is `unknown`; carry all prior entries and never bind a later batch |
| CONSULT COVERAGE | actual decision/boundary coverage -> batch ID; list unanswered questions. A partial report can consume capacity without clearing a required review |
| CONSULT HISTORY | every attempt, newest first: batch ID, trigger, attempt, executing provider, advisor provider/model/effort, CLI or harness transport, diversity (cross-provider/same-provider fallback/unknown), sanitized command or spawn specification/child ID, observed exit status or harness terminal state, failure reason, report status (`none`, `partial`, `complete`), actual coverage, and counter changes. Reasons include usage limit/429, auth, launch, provider, timeout, incomplete, cancelled; no invented exit codes or token usage. Preserve prior failures and evidence required to reconsider routes. Cite `$PROMPT` literally; never contents/secrets |
| DELEGATION STATE | worker/advisor role, task-owned worktree paths/branches, worker liveness, integration commits, preserved work, cleanup complete or blocked with reason/recovery path; `none` if unused |
| WHY | header only: why this model and effort. If the declared plan allowance or an observed usage limit changed the order of comparable routes, say which |
| PROMPT | fenced `md`; begins with the exact active-workflow and mandatory-skill lines; contains receiving stage, exposure/shape, task and complete budget/grant/history/delegation state without relying on the short header; excludes model recommendations and WHY; self-contained; no `PASTE BACK` |

Every handoff names the next `/handoff` in `EXPECTED OUTPUT` — except Verify Implementation, which offers Plan Next Version instead. A handoff missing that is incomplete.

Keep historical executing-provider identity inside advisor attempt records where needed to establish diversity; it is not the receiver’s identity. Ordinary sender identity does not belong in the prompt.

Launching a stage owner via {{if .Both}}`codex exec` or `claude -p`{{else if .Claude}}`claude -p`{{else}}`codex exec`{{end}}: pass the entire fenced `PROMPT:`, from `HANDOFF WORKFLOW` through `EXPECTED OUTPUT`. A consult call instead receives only the compact batch packet required by the `consult` skill.

## Implement → Verify

The verifier has no shared context — anything omitted is unavailable to it. The prompt must carry:

- what changed, by functional area
- exact files to inspect
- checks passed / failed / blocked, and why blocked ones are environmental rather than implementation failures
- committed / uncommitted / staged state
- commit hash, or the exact no-commit reason
- residual risks

## Next handoff

| Completing | `NEXT HANDOFF TO WRITE` / `EXPECTED OUTPUT` |
|---|---|
| Plan | `/handoff` Verify Plan |
| Verify Plan | `/handoff` Implement |
| Implement | `/handoff` Verify Implementation, or Fix if the retry failed |
| Verify Implementation | offer only: `Next handoff available: Plan Next Version — <one phrase>` |
| Fix | `/handoff` Verify Implementation |
| Plan Next Version | `/handoff` Plan, or `DONE: no further handoff recommended` |
